## Security Audit Checklist

- ✅ **No token, key, or PII written to cleartext store** - Refresh token in SecureStore, access token in memory only
- ✅ **No vendor credential in anything that ships** - All payment processing goes through our backend gateway
- ✅ **No TLS weakening, no cleartext HTTP** - HTTPS enforced, no certificate bypass
- ✅ **Every incoming URL passes allowlist resolver** - Session IDs validated server-side, no client-side trust
- ✅ **Security-relevant decisions stated** - Payment gateway architecture, token storage strategy, input validation

## Key Security Decisions

1. **Payment processing through backend gateway** - The app never calls the payment provider directly; all requests go through our authenticated backend (§3)
2. **Token storage** - Refresh token in SecureStore (device-only), access token in memory only (§1)
3. **Input validation** - Amount and currency validated client-side for UX, re-validated server-side for security (§3)
4. **Session management** - Checkout sessions created server-side with proper authorization checks (§4)
